  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S. Jrj Foods Private Limited vs Union Of India on 8 September, 2022 Author: Dinesh Mehta Bench: Dinesh Mehta (1 of 2) [Crlw-274/2022] High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan At Jodhpur S. B. Criminal Writ Petition No. 274/2022 M/s. Jrj Foods Private Limited, 314, 315 Phase-1 Chhatral Tal, Kalol, Dist. Gandhi Nagar-382729 Gujarat Through Authorized Legal Representative Of",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "2. While informing that the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 had actually come into force after the Food Safety and Standards (Licensing and Registration of Food Business) Regulations, 2011 were published on 01.08.2011, learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the State has decided to withdraw prosecution under the Act of 1954 in a number of cases but the same is being done selectively and not in all cases. 3. Learned counsel submits that the petitioner, resident of Gujarat, is facing the trial in a case, which cannot continue, as the Act of 2006 does not provide prosecution in case of misbranded goods.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "2. While informing that the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 had actually come into force after the Food Safety and Standards (Licensing and Registration of Food Business) Regulations, 2011 were published on 01.08.2011, learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the State has decided to withdraw prosecution under the Act of 1954 in a number of cases but the same is being done selectively and not in all cases. 3. Learned counsel submits that the petitioner, resident of Gujarat, is facing the trial in a case, which cannot continue, as the Act of 2006 does not provide prosecution in case of misbranded goods.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
